508
00:19:56,679 --> 00:19:57,420
point one.

509
00:19:57,600 --> 00:19:59,150
By our arithmetic,

510
00:19:59,150 --> 00:20:02,252
the F5's best published speed is one

511
00:20:02,252 --> 00:20:04,406
point one miles per hour,

512
00:20:04,406 --> 00:20:07,766
or about one point eight kilometres per

513
00:20:07,766 --> 00:20:10,092
hour, above the Venom GT's.

514
00:20:10,441 --> 00:20:13,461
So the F5's best published top speed

515
00:20:13,461 --> 00:20:16,480
is barely above the car it replaced,

516
00:20:16,480 --> 00:20:19,834
which ran its record in twenty fourteen.

517
00:20:20,014 --> 00:20:22,227
That is not a criticism of the

518
00:20:22,227 --> 00:20:22,522
car.

519
00:20:22,702 --> 00:20:25,722
Different runs have different lengths of road,

520
00:20:25,722 --> 00:20:27,691
and Motor One does not say how

521
00:20:27,691 --> 00:20:30,121
long the February twenty-two run had.

522
00:20:30,301 --> 00:20:32,267
It is a reminder that a top

523
00:20:32,267 --> 00:20:34,816
speed depends on the runway as much

524
00:20:34,816 --> 00:20:36,054
as on the engine,

525
00:20:36,054 --> 00:20:38,021
a point we return to in the

526
00:20:38,021 --> 00:20:38,822
next video.

527
00:20:39,173 --> 00:20:41,414
If you read a hypercar claim,

528
00:20:41,414 --> 00:20:44,815
here are four questions this video suggests.

529
00:20:44,995 --> 00:20:46,894
Is it a measured speed or a

530
00:20:46,894 --> 00:20:47,387
target?

531
00:20:47,567 --> 00:20:49,851
Is it one direction or a two-way

532
00:20:49,851 --> 00:20:50,423
average?

533
00:20:50,603 --> 00:20:52,158
Which fuel was used?

534
00:20:52,338 --> 00:20:54,351
And how many cars were built,

535
00:20:54,351 --> 00:20:55,392
by whose count?

536
00:20:55,572 --> 00:20:58,176
The Venom GT failed the record test

537
00:20:58,176 --> 00:20:59,367
on two of those,

538
00:20:59,367 --> 00:21:01,227
and the F5 so far has not

539
00:21:01,227 --> 00:21:03,757
published the answer to the first.

540
00:21:03,937 --> 00:21:06,300
They are fair questions for every car

541
00:21:06,300 --> 00:21:07,257
in this series.

542
00:21:07,608 --> 00:21:08,769
What we could not find.

543
00:21:08,949 --> 00:21:11,617
A verified top speed above three hundred

544
00:21:11,617 --> 00:21:12,617
miles per hour.

545
00:21:12,797 --> 00:21:15,916
The number of F5s delivered to customers,

546
00:21:15,916 --> 00:21:18,577
because evo says only that cars are

547
00:21:18,577 --> 00:21:20,555
being built and delivered,

548
00:21:20,555 --> 00:21:21,772
without a count.

549
00:21:21,952 --> 00:21:24,785
The fuel behind the headline power figure.

550
00:21:24,965 --> 00:21:26,764
The cost of ownership.

551
00:21:26,944 --> 00:21:29,498
And whether the crashed car was repaired.

552
00:21:29,678 --> 00:21:31,838
We will not guess any of them.

553
00:21:32,188 --> 00:21:34,370
So the two secrets stand.

554
00:21:34,550 --> 00:21:36,711
The name comes from the top of

555
00:21:36,711 --> 00:21:38,008
the tornado scale,

556
00:21:38,008 --> 00:21:40,818
and the headline horsepower is only one

557
00:21:40,818 --> 00:21:42,979
